<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 23,891,000 bushels -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 23,891,000 bushels -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors</p>
<p>Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members</p>
<p>(crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 07/23/97    07/16/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 23,891,000  21,871,000    23,614,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  57,779	41,782	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   07/23/97    07/16/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   7,002,000   3,479,000     4,312,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,288,000   4,262,000     4,384,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,483,000   3,378,000     3,413,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,339,000   1,744,000     2,072,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  2,720,000   3,016,000     3,077,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,635,000   4,395,000     4,793,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,598,000   1,597,000     1,563,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	23,891,000  21,871,000    23,614,000</p>
